{
    "background_story": "Freya was a skilled blacksmith in a small Viking village. She spent most of her days hammering away at the anvil, shaping metal into powerful swords and shields for the village warriors. But Freya's true passion was crafting intricate armor, particularly the gird that protected a warrior's waist. She took great pride in her work, carefully weaving leather straps and metal plates into a strong yet flexible design. When the village chieftain's son, Erik, was preparing for battle, he sought out Freya's expertise. She crafted a magnificent gird that would protect him from even the most ferocious attacks. Erik returned victorious, crediting Freya's gird for saving his life. From that day on, Freya was known as the village's most skilled armor-maker, and her girds were sought after by warriors from all over the land.",
